OL,4,CBlair's account of Brown 'unfair'
OL,5, Allies of Gordon Brown have rallied
OL,6, behind the former prime minister,
OL,7, describing criticism of him by Tony
OL,8, Blair as "unfair" and "one-sided".
OL,10,FIn his memoirs, Mr Blair said his
OL,11,Fsuccessor was "maddening" and suggested
OL,12,FLabour lost power because Mr Brown
OL,13,Fbacked away from reforms he had begun.
OL,15,FFormer deputy leader Lord Prescott said
OL,16,FMr Brown had faced the worst financial
OL,17,Fcrisis in generations.
OL,19,FTwo Labour leadership candidates also
OL,20,Fcriticised Mr Blair's account.
OL,22,D]C This Ceefax page is from 01-09-10
OL,23,S]D Much more at: teletextarchive.com
